---
description: TubeWriter plugin architecture and safety rules
alwaysApply: true
---

Read CLAUDE.md in the plugin root before changing anything. It is the full architecture doc.

Non-negotiable safety rules for this codebase:

- Nothing writes to YouTube except TW_Plan::publish() and TW_Plan::restore(), and both save a TW_History backup first.
- Never add calls to videos.delete, playlists.delete or playlistItems.delete.
- videos.update clears any writable field you leave out of a part you send. Always go through TW_YouTube::write_video(), which sends every writable field.
- Only send the status part when changing the schedule, and copy every writable status field from the live video.
- Publish must keep the review fingerprint check, the step 6 checkbox and the confirm() pop-up.
- Any new editor field must call staleReview() on change so step 6 re-locks until a fresh review.
- Game title and end screens have no API. Keep them as manual Studio steps.

Style: plain PHP and vanilla JS, no build step, WordPress APIs, escape all output, check capability and nonce on every handler. UI copy uses no em dashes and no semicolons.
